{% doc %}
  Outputs the theme's built-in copy for a page, or nothing when the handle is
  not one it knows.

  A theme cannot create pages, so every store still needs the page itself. It
  can supply what goes inside it, which is the part that would otherwise be
  pasted in by hand on every store. Create a page with the right handle, leave
  the body empty, and the document appears.

  Anything typed into the page body replaces this — that is the edit path, and
  it is per store. Editing the page-body snippets changes every store on the
  next theme upload.

  @param {string} handle - The page handle, usually page.handle.

  @example
  {% capture body %}{% render 'page-default', handle: page.handle %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Aliases match the lists the footer resolves links with, so a store that
    names its return policy "returns" gets the document too. Exact handles
    only: a blank page called "shipping-information" should stay blank rather
    than sprout a shipping policy nobody asked for.
  endcomment
  assign lookup = handle | strip | downcase
  assign key = ''

  assign groups = 'privacy=privacy-policy|privacy;refund=refund-policy|return-policy|returns|return-and-refund-policy;shipping=shipping-policy|shipping|delivery-policy;payment=payment-policy|payments|payment-information;terms=terms-of-service|terms|terms-and-conditions;about=about-us|about|our-story|about-me' | split: ';'

  if lookup != blank
    for group in groups
      assign parts = group | split: '='
      assign group_aliases = parts[1] | split: '|'
      for group_alias in group_aliases
        if group_alias == lookup
          assign key = parts[0]
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if key != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{%- case key -%}
  {%- when 'privacy' -%}{% render 'page-body-privacy' %}
  {%- when 'refund' -%}{% render 'page-body-refund' %}
  {%- when 'shipping' -%}{% render 'page-body-shipping' %}
  {%- when 'payment' -%}{% render 'page-body-payment' %}
  {%- when 'terms' -%}{% render 'page-body-terms' %}
  {%- when 'about' -%}{% render 'page-body-about' %}
{%- endcase -%}
